1. Are there further improvements worth making?

Yes — but they are second-order improvements, not corrections. They fall into three buckets:

Make certain comparisons visually undeniable

Refine a few comparison choices to avoid subtle methodological criticism

Improve readability by collapsing some text into tables/figures

Nothing here threatens validity; these are about maximising clarity and examiner confidence.

2. What would benefit most from additional or improved visualisation?

You already have many good figures. The remaining gap is that some of your strongest claims are still numerically proven rather than visually obvious. Examiners tend to trust figures more than tables.

