2.2 Effect sizes are crying out for a forest plot
Problem

You report very large Cohen’s d values (correctly caveated), but in table form they:

Look abstract

Invite “n is small” criticism

🔹 Recommended figure

Effect size forest plot:

Y-axis: Comparison (Kyber vs RSA, Kyber vs ECDHE, etc.)

X-axis: Cohen’s d

Horizontal CI bars (bootstrapped if available)

Why this helps

Visually communicates magnitude dominance

Shows that effects are not borderline

Reinforces that even with small n, effects are overwhelming

This is PhD-level statistical communication and examiners notice.

