4. Are you comparing things the right way around?
Short answer

Mostly yes — but two subtle refinements would make it bullet-proof.

4.1 The “aggregate classical” baseline is slightly risky

You use:

“PQC vs Classical (aggregate)”

Why this can be questioned

Classical algorithms serve different roles

Aggregation can hide structure

An examiner may ask:
“Which classical primitive exactly?”

🔹 Improvement (simple, not disruptive)

Always pair:

Kyber ↔ ECDHE

Dilithium ↔ ECDSA

RSA used as a legacy baseline only

You already do this implicitly — just make it explicit in framing.

📌 Suggestion:
Rename:

“PQC vs Classical (aggregate)” →
“PQC vs selected classical baselines (role-aligned)”

4.2 Throughput comparisons need one extra guardrail

You explain throughput vs latency very well, but one number is still risky:

GCP throughput is much higher

An examiner might say:

“Isn’t this just because you have more cores?”

🔹 Improvement

Add one normalised metric:

Throughput per vCPU

Or messages/sec/core

This instantly defuses the criticism and strengthens your cloud analysis.

